# .graphifyignore — extra scan excludes for graphify, on top of .gitignore.
#
# gitignore syntax. graphify reads .gitignore FIRST and this file LAST, and the
# merge is exclude-only: a `!` re-include here can NOT bring back anything
# .gitignore already dropped. Only ever add excludes below.
#
# Already handled elsewhere — do not repeat here:
#   .gitignore      implementation-notes/ docs/superpowers/ and the generated
#                   *-flowchart/-codewalk/-plan-deck/-component/-sequence/-c4 HTML
#   graphify built-in  graphify-out/ .graphify/ node_modules/ .git/ dist/ build/
#                      __pycache__/ .venv/ and the usual cache dirs

# Per-run job output — timestamped run transcripts and state, regenerated by
# tooling, never source. A prior run of this dir carried 1197 files / ~1.5M words,
# which pushed the corpus past graphify's 500-file gate on its own.
jobs/
plugins/lirbox/skills/*/harbor/tasks/*/environment/skill/

# NOTE: skills/*/evals/fixtures/ is deliberately NOT excluded. Those are
# single-line mutations of a clean baseline, each pinning one validator rule, and
# the extraction maps each fixture to the rule it violates. That is real signal.
